WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:04.800
In this era of major movie studios earmarking
their spots on the release schedule years

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:09.650
ahead of time, it isn't too early to start
making box office predictions for 2018.

00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:14.110
Among the already dozens of promising projects
slated for release, here are some of the movies

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:16.230
we're projecting to hit big.

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:17.780
Black Panther

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:22.580
Before we finally get to Avengers: Infinity
War, the Marvel Cinematic Universe is going

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:29.260
to make a quick stop in Wakanda, home of everybody's
favorite superpowered feline: the Black Panther.

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:34.000
In the his first standalone film, T'Challa
has returned home after his dad's tragic death

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:39.440
in Captain America: Civil War, and now he's
set to rule his technological wonderland.

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:43.730
Unfortunately, according to the official plot
description, the new king will find himself

00:00:43.730 --> 00:00:45.809
facing "a powerful old enemy."

00:00:45.809 --> 00:00:48.960
Black Panther prowls into theaters February
16th.

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:50.100
"Let's have some fun."

00:00:57.240 --> 00:00:58.220
Tomb Raider

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:04.530
Alicia Vikander is taking the place of Angelina
Jolie, starring as one of the greatest video

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:07.620
game characters of all time: Lara Croft.

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:12.330
In the reboot, Croft is a bike courier inspired
by video messages from her late father to

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:17.680
journey into the jungle and find the mysterious
"Mother of Death," a tomb that might end the

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:18.710
world if opened.

00:01:18.710 --> 00:01:22.680
Unfortunately for Croft, she's not the only
one interested in the tomb.

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:26.930
With an Oscar winning actress as the lead,
we're pretty psyched to see the new Lara Croft

00:01:26.930 --> 00:01:30.140
raid movie theaters everywhere come March
16th.

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:32.350
Pacific Rim: Uprising

00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:37.430
The Pan Pacific Defense Corps is gearing up
for a rematch in Pacific Rim: Uprising.

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:42.820
Sadly, Guillermo del Toro will only be producing
this time, but the science fiction spectacle

00:01:42.820 --> 00:01:44.990
is in incredibly capable hands.

00:01:44.990 --> 00:01:50.580
The sequel will be directed by Steven S. DeKnight—the
guy in charge of Spartacus and Daredevil—and

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:54.250
the film will star John Boyega from the new
Star Wars trilogy.

00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:59.170
If you're psyched for two hours of Kaiju-killing
fun, get ready to cancel the apocalypse on

00:01:59.170 --> 00:02:01.390
March 23rd.

00:02:01.390 --> 00:02:03.009
Ready Player One

00:02:03.009 --> 00:02:07.790
Based on the bestselling novel by Ernest Cline,
Ready Player One looks like the ultimate pop

00:02:07.790 --> 00:02:09.159
culture mash-up.

00:02:09.159 --> 00:02:13.840
The plot features elements from games like
Overwatch and Street Fighter as well as every

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:19.249
'80s movie imaginable, including Tron, Akira,
and A Nightmare on Elm Street.

00:02:19.249 --> 00:02:25.319
And, of course, it's directed by the king
of 1980s cinema himself: Steven Spielberg.

00:02:25.319 --> 00:02:29.720
In addition to all the orcs and DeLoreans,
the plot will focus on a young kid named Wade

00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:35.329
Watts who escapes his impoverished life by
retreating into the OASIS, the ultimate virtual

00:02:35.329 --> 00:02:36.329
reality world.

00:02:36.329 --> 00:02:37.340
Ready Player One will race into theaters on
March 20th.

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:38.900
New Mutants

00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:43.239
Now that the X-Men movies have exhausted pretty
much every timeline they can leap into and

00:02:43.239 --> 00:02:47.790
out of with Logan's dismal glimpse of the
future, it's time for the New Mutants to start

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:49.129
running the school.

00:02:49.129 --> 00:02:53.859
New Mutants will likely introduce a bevy of
new talented teens who, as in the comic spinoff

00:02:53.859 --> 00:02:59.269
series of the same name, are trained by Charles
Xavier to emerge as a new class of heroes.

00:02:59.269 --> 00:03:03.280
It remains to be seen which of the comics'
most fascinating kids will make it into the

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:08.389
new generation of the X-Men film series, but
we'll find out on April 13th when New Mutants

00:03:08.389 --> 00:03:10.459
hits theaters.

00:03:10.459 --> 00:03:12.180
Super Troopers 2

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:17.030
When Super Troopers came out in 2001, the
cop comedy failed to impress critics, but

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:20.569
over the years, it's morphed into a genuine
cult classic.

00:03:20.569 --> 00:03:25.230
Seventeen years and one successful Indiegogo
campaign later, it looks like the members

00:03:25.230 --> 00:03:29.249
of Broken Lizard will finally bring their
prankster patrolmen back to the big screen

00:03:29.249 --> 00:03:30.989
on April 20th.

00:03:30.989 --> 00:03:35.099
According to Entertainment Weekly, the plot
will focus on the original five troopers as

00:03:35.099 --> 00:03:40.279
they're "called in to set up a new Highway
Patrol Station in an area at the center of

00:03:40.279 --> 00:03:42.680
a border dispute between the U.S. and Canada."

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:44.909
Avengers: Infinity War

00:03:44.909 --> 00:03:50.670
In 2008, Tony Stark launched the Marvel Cinematic
Universe when he built a robot suit, beat

00:03:50.670 --> 00:03:55.349
up a bunch of terrorists, and boldly declared,
"I am Iron Man."

00:03:55.349 --> 00:03:59.969
Since then, moviegoers have been introduced
to a whole host of superheroes, as well as

00:03:59.969 --> 00:04:03.969
a collection of mysterious stones that keep
popping up across the universe.

00:04:03.969 --> 00:04:09.479
And now, 18 movies later, all our heroes are
going to converge in one epic battle against

00:04:09.479 --> 00:04:14.919
the biggest bad guy in the galaxy, a space
titan with the world's deadliest fashion accessory.

00:04:14.919 --> 00:04:20.970
Avengers: Infinity War is the ultimate cinematic
crossover — jump into the fray on May 4th.

00:04:20.970 --> 00:04:23.560
Solo: A Star Wars Story

00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:29.659
Ron Howard's Solo: A Star Wars Story promises
fans the origin story of everyone's favorite

00:04:29.659 --> 00:04:31.639
scruffy-looking nerf herder.

00:04:31.639 --> 00:04:37.169
Plot details are a little scarce, but we do
know Alden Ehrenreich stars as Han Solo, Donald

00:04:37.169 --> 00:04:42.470
Glover will appear as Lando, Woody Harrelson
will star as Han's mentor Beckett, and we'll

00:04:42.470 --> 00:04:46.879
get to see Han meet up with Chewbacca and
become a snarky space cowboy.

00:04:46.879 --> 00:04:51.889
Rest assured, this space opera will make a
truckload of cash — and rile up the fanbase,

00:04:51.889 --> 00:04:55.250
for better or for worse — come May 25th.

00:04:55.250 --> 00:04:56.860
Deadpool 2

00:04:56.860 --> 00:05:02.770
When Deadpool hit theaters in 2016, it grossed
around $783 million dollars and became the

00:05:02.770 --> 00:05:06.030
highest-grossing R-rated movie in cinematic
history.

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:11.190
The sequel has a lot to live up to, but Deadpool
2 looks like a lot of foul-mouthed fun, with

00:05:11.190 --> 00:05:12.819
a dynamite cast.

00:05:12.819 --> 00:05:15.569
There's also some impressive talent behind
the camera.

00:05:15.569 --> 00:05:19.280
After original director Tim Miller left the
project over creative differences with Ryan

00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:24.710
Reynolds, he was replaced by David Leitch,
best known for co-directing John Wick.

00:05:24.710 --> 00:05:29.150
Deadpool 2 is set to smash through the fourth
wall on June 1st.

00:05:29.150 --> 00:05:34.660
"Remember: this is your world, so you get
to make and break the rules here."

00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:37.050
Jurassic World: Fallen Kingdom

00:05:37.050 --> 00:05:42.389
When Jurassic World roared into theaters in
2016, it quickly became the fourth highest-grossing

00:05:42.389 --> 00:05:47.690
film of all time, raking in approximately
$1.6 billion dollars.

00:05:47.690 --> 00:05:51.740
With that kind of success, we all knew it
was only a matter of time before we went back

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:53.360
to that dino-infested island.

00:05:53.360 --> 00:05:58.759
And now, with Jurassic World: Fallen Kingdom,
not only will we get to see raptors run amok,

00:05:58.759 --> 00:06:02.939
but we'll also watch an abandoned theme park
get blown to smithereens.

00:06:02.939 --> 00:06:07.500
This guaranteed blockbuster promises to be
an over-the-top spectacle — catch it June

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:08.719
22nd.

00:06:08.719 --> 00:06:10.949
The Purge: The Island

00:06:10.949 --> 00:06:15.659
The Purge franchise has been picking off victims
and making political points since 2013, but

00:06:15.659 --> 00:06:18.949
have you ever wondered how this night of bloodshed
started?

00:06:18.949 --> 00:06:23.349
We'll finally get an answer to that question
with The Purge: The Island, the fourth film

00:06:23.349 --> 00:06:26.009
in the series and the very first prequel.

00:06:26.009 --> 00:06:30.699
Written by franchise mastermind James DeMonaco,
the newest film will take place before the

00:06:30.699 --> 00:06:32.490
Ethan Hawke original.

00:06:32.490 --> 00:06:35.110
It's set to hit theaters on July 4th.

00:06:35.110 --> 00:06:36.699
Ant-Man and the Wasp

00:06:36.699 --> 00:06:42.410
Audiences are in for a marvelous time when
Ant-Man and the Wasp arrives July 6th. Paul

00:06:42.410 --> 00:06:46.419
Rudd and Evangeline Lilly will be suiting
up as the namesake heroes, and they'll be

00:06:46.419 --> 00:06:50.520
joined by an impressive cast of familiar faces
and newcomers alike.

00:06:50.520 --> 00:06:55.779
But most interestingly, Michelle Pfeiffer
is switching sides, abandoning DC and Catwoman

00:06:55.779 --> 00:06:59.010
to play Janet Van Dyne, the original Wasp.

00:06:59.010 --> 00:07:03.610
In the first Ant-Man, we learned that Janet
was lost inside the quantum realm, but now

00:07:03.610 --> 00:07:09.379
it looks like Ant-Man and the Wasp will somehow
rescue her from her decades-long adventure.

00:07:09.379 --> 00:07:10.650
The Nun

00:07:10.650 --> 00:07:15.449
The Conjuring series is quickly making its
case that horror movie franchises can be extended

00:07:15.449 --> 00:07:17.169
universes too.

00:07:17.169 --> 00:07:21.210
Following in the success of Annabelle, the
franchise's first spin-off, producers have

00:07:21.210 --> 00:07:26.099
tapped actress Bonnie Aarons to reprise her
role as the Demon Nun from The Conjuring 2

00:07:26.099 --> 00:07:30.000
in her own spinoff, titled simply The Nun.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:31.800
Catch it July 13th.

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:34.360
Alita: Battle Angel

00:07:34.360 --> 00:07:40.499
Ever since the '90s, James Cameron has wanted
to adapt Gunnm, a popular Japanese manga.

00:07:40.499 --> 00:07:45.150
But now that he's preoccupied with the Avatar
sequels, Cameron has drafted Robert Rodriguez

00:07:45.150 --> 00:07:46.699
to work on the project.

00:07:46.699 --> 00:07:52.469
As a result, we've got Alita: Battle Angel,
a sci-fi adventure starring Rosa Salazar as

00:07:52.469 --> 00:07:57.909
a cyborg with amazing martial arts prowess
and controversially large eyes.

00:07:57.909 --> 00:08:01.900
Cameron will finally see his passion project
in theaters on July 20th.

00:08:01.900 --> 00:08:04.469
Mission: Impossible 6

00:08:04.469 --> 00:08:09.360
Christopher McQuarrie returns to helm a sixth
installment to the covert op action-adventure

00:08:09.360 --> 00:08:13.930
series, and while details are scant as to
what the actual storyline will be, we know

00:08:13.930 --> 00:08:17.680
the film will delve deeper into Ethan Hunt's
backstory.

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:22.900
Cruise trained for a year to prepare for some
truly insane action sequences as Hunt, and

00:08:22.900 --> 00:08:27.789
we can't wait until July 27th to see how the
movie star puts his life on the line this

00:08:27.789 --> 00:08:28.840
time.

00:08:28.840 --> 00:08:30.069
The Predator

00:08:30.069 --> 00:08:35.620
Kicking off a new round of interplanetary
big game hunting, The Predator finds writer-director

00:08:35.620 --> 00:08:40.829
Shane Black—who made a blink-and-you'll-miss-it
appearance in the 1987 original—making a

00:08:40.829 --> 00:08:43.229
long-overdue return to the franchise.

00:08:43.229 --> 00:08:48.690
The latest addition to the series works as
kind of a sequel and follows a group of PTSD-stricken

00:08:48.690 --> 00:08:53.579
soldiers who band together to kill the spine-crackl
ing alien hunters.

00:08:53.579 --> 00:08:58.449
Expect our ragtag heroes to face off against
everyone's favorite skull collector on August

00:08:58.449 --> 00:08:59.459
3rd.

00:08:59.459 --> 00:09:01.480
The Equalizer 2

00:09:01.480 --> 00:09:05.750
On August 3rd, Denzel Washington returns for
The Equalizer 2.

00:09:05.750 --> 00:09:09.940
The actor is making history here, starring
in his very first sequel.

00:09:09.940 --> 00:09:14.440
There aren't a lot of plot details out there,
but come on, we're going to see Denzel Washington

00:09:14.440 --> 00:09:17.560
destroy a bunch of bad guys in incredibly
creative ways.

00:09:17.560 --> 00:09:19.820
What more do you need to know?

00:09:19.820 --> 00:09:20.839
Venom

00:09:20.839 --> 00:09:26.260
Sony's plans for a Spider-Man cinematic universe
seemed to hit the skids when the studio abandoned

00:09:26.260 --> 00:09:31.970
its Andrew Garfield-led Amazing Spider-Man
franchise in favor of another reboot, teaming

00:09:31.970 --> 00:09:36.540
up with Marvel for joint custody of the character's
film rights and putting Tom Holland in the

00:09:36.540 --> 00:09:38.470
web-slinger's duds.

00:09:38.470 --> 00:09:43.790
While the Sinister Six movie might still be
dead, Venom is officially back on the schedule:

00:09:43.790 --> 00:09:49.110
the alien symbiote anti-hero is now slated
to sling his way into theaters on October

00:09:49.110 --> 00:09:52.290
5th with Tom Hardy in the title role.

00:09:52.290 --> 00:09:53.720
Halloween

00:09:53.720 --> 00:09:58.350
Once again starring Jamie Lee Curtis, the
latest entry in the Halloween franchise will

00:09:58.350 --> 00:10:01.740
ignore every film except for the original.

00:10:01.740 --> 00:10:06.791
Cult comedy mainstays David Gordon Green and
Danny McBride are behind the sequel, which

00:10:06.791 --> 00:10:10.630
is supposedly going to be the last Halloween
movie ever.

00:10:10.630 --> 00:10:15.029
But just like Michael Myers, we suspect the
series will eventually come back to life.

00:10:15.029 --> 00:10:18.199
Catch the horror on October 19th.

00:10:18.199 --> 00:10:20.940
Fantastic Beasts: The Crimes of Grindelwald

00:10:20.940 --> 00:10:21.940
J.K.

00:10:21.940 --> 00:10:26.880
Rowling's Harry Potter spin-off series Fantastic
Beasts and Where to Find Them is on deck for

00:10:26.880 --> 00:10:32.570
its second installment on November 16th, following
Newt Scamander and his pals on another adventure

00:10:32.570 --> 00:10:35.120
in the world of witchcraft and wizardry.

00:10:35.120 --> 00:10:40.149
The sequel will feature a young Albus Dumbledore,
played by Jude Law, who instructs our hero

00:10:40.149 --> 00:10:45.990
to chase down and apprehend Gellert Grindelwald,
a villainous wizard guilty of magical crimes

00:10:45.990 --> 00:10:47.430
played by Johnny Depp.

00:10:47.430 --> 00:10:52.000
The film promises to begin the battle for
the ages between the esteemed professor and

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:54.320
his former bestie-gone-rogue.

00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:56.800
Spider-Man: Into the Spider-Verse

00:10:56.800 --> 00:11:01.949
Ever since Miles Morales first appeared back
in 2011, Marvel fans have desperately wanted

00:11:01.949 --> 00:11:04.230
to see him get his own Spider-Man movie.

00:11:04.230 --> 00:11:10.740
On December 14th Sony plans on releasing Spider-Man:
Into the Spider-Verse, an animated adventure

00:11:10.740 --> 00:11:13.889
following the young web-slinger as he fights
crime.

00:11:13.889 --> 00:11:18.899
Phil Lord and Chris Miller of The Lego Movie
are credited as executive producers, and Lord

00:11:18.899 --> 00:11:23.740
penned the screenplay, so expect to see his
unique brand of humor swinging across the

00:11:23.740 --> 00:11:24.460
screen.

00:11:24.460 --> 00:11:26.260
"Wait, so how many of us are there?"

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:30.850
Aquaman

00:11:30.850 --> 00:11:35.009
The introduction of Arthur "Aquaman" Curry
in Batman versus Superman: Dawn of Justice

00:11:35.009 --> 00:11:39.589
was but a taste of what was to come from Jason
Momoa as the trident-wielding hero in Justice

00:11:39.589 --> 00:11:40.620
League.

00:11:40.620 --> 00:11:46.830
With 2018's Aquaman, he'll embrace his destiny
as the heir to the kingdom of Atlantis.

00:11:46.830 --> 00:11:51.649
Director James Wan helms the watery actioner
that will follow Curry's life from boyhood

00:11:51.649 --> 00:11:56.440
to kinghood, and Dolph Lundgren will show
up as a powerful Atlantean king.

00:11:56.440 --> 00:12:01.620
That means on December 21st, we're getting
a film with both Ivan Drago and Khal Drogo,

00:12:01.620 --> 00:12:05.240
which might be way too much muscle for one
movie to handle.

00:12:05.240 --> 00:12:06.370
Thanks for watching!

00:12:06.370 --> 00:12:08.839
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:12:08.839 --> 00:12:11.040
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

